{
  "about": "House rules for the nikud pipeline (tools/nikud/lib/house.mjs). A matching rule is a 5th, overriding vote: precedence is decision > house rule > vote, and a word a rule decides never reaches disagreements.json. 'word'/'wordRe' match the whole bare word; 'before'/'after' are regexes on the bare item text before/after the word. First match wins, so context rules come first. Words with two common readings (את, אם, עם, אל, שם, פה, לך, שלך, למה, אילו, שני, חצי (חֵצִי / construct חֲצִי), אלה (also the girl's name אֵלָה in the word problems), היו, קראו, ענו, השלימו, הקיפו, שאלה, כתוב, עולה, בשעה, בשבוע, ו־digit) are deliberately NOT here. Dagesh follows the project spec (kal and chazak everywhere) even where the booklet drops dagesh chazak (it prints הַמִילָה, הַשְׁאֵלוֹת, שֶׁלִפְנֵיכֶם, בַּתַרְגִילִים), so the booklet settles VOWELS only. Every form was checked against Dicta, GPT and Claude on 103 real/crafted sentences (tools/nikud README, house rules).",
  "rules": [
    { "id": "prefix-before-digit", "wordRe": "^[בלכ]$", "after": "^[־-]\\d", "forms": { "ב": "בְּ", "ל": "לְ", "כ": "כְּ" },
      "reason": "A one-letter prefix glued to a number by a maqaf takes sheva, whatever the number word (booklet: בְּ־8, בְּ־2 תַּבְנִיּוֹת, לְ־12).", "source": "booklet pp.11-12; planner" },
    { "id": "beshura-n", "expectDissent": true, "word": "בשורה", "after": "^\\s*\\d", "form": "בְּשׁוּרָה",
      "reason": "\"בשורה N\" is indefinite: בְּשׁוּרָה 2 כָּתוּב. Both LLMs wrote בַּשּׁוּרָה; Dicta was right.", "source": "booklet pp.8, 9; planner" },
    { "id": "beshurot-n", "expectDissent": true, "word": "בשורות", "after": "^\\s*\\d", "form": "בְּשׁוּרוֹת",
      "reason": "Same as בשורה N, plural: בְּשׁוּרוֹת 5–3.", "source": "booklet p.7" },
    { "id": "katuv-after-line", "word": "כתוב", "before": "(בשורה|בשורות|שורה)\\s*[\\d\\s–\\-]+[:,]?\\s*$", "form": "כָּתוּב",
      "reason": "After \"בשורה N\" it is the participle כָּתוּב (\"it says\"), not the imperative כְּתוֹב.", "source": "booklet pp.8, 9" },
    { "id": "shura", "word": "שורה", "form": "שׁוּרָה", "reason": "Only one reading.", "source": "booklet p.9 (שׁוּרָה 22)" },

    { "id": "mah", "expectDissent": true, "word": "מה", "form": "מָה", "reason": "Project style: מָה everywhere, also before a guttural (no מֶה).", "source": "booklet p.8 מָה פֵּירוּשׁ; planner" },
    { "id": "umah", "expectDissent": true, "word": "ומה", "form": "וּמָה", "reason": "ו before מ is וּ; מָה as above.", "source": "planner (מָה)" },
